Pocket Casts for iOS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of the following Autohop source files are derived from or
architecturally based on Pocket Casts for iOS:

  - Autohop/Playback/SilenceDetector.swift
      Derived from: podcasts/AudioReadTask.swift
      Nature: Direct algorithmic port. The RMS threshold constants, gap-size
      thresholds, re-insert counts, last-5-seconds guard, overflow safety cap,
      and fade-in/fade-out join logic are ported from the Pocket Casts
      implementation. The code has been restructured into a Swift value-type
      struct and adapted to the Autohop buffer pipeline.

  - Autohop/Models/SilenceGapAccounting.swift
      Derived from: podcasts/AudioReadTask.swift
      Nature: Direct algorithmic port. The gap-size thresholds and re-insert
      counts (extracted from SilenceDetector.swift as a pure, headlessly
      testable value type) are ported from the Pocket Casts implementation.

  - Autohop/Playback/PlaybackEngine.swift
      Derived from: podcasts/EffectsPlayer.swift
      Nature: Architectural derivation. The vocal boost signal chain
      (high-pass filter → dynamics processor → peak limiter, using Apple
      system Audio Units) follows the architecture of the Pocket Casts
      implementation. No source code is copied verbatim.

  - Autohop/Playback/SleepTimerService.swift
  - Autohop/Views/SleepTimerSheetView.swift
      Derived from: (none — original Autohop code)
      Nature: The concept and general feature set of the sleep timer (duration
      presets, end-of-episode mode, episode count, 5-second fade-out, and
      5-minute auto-restart window) were informed by studying the Pocket Casts
      iOS implementation. No source code, constants, or algorithms have been
      ported. The countdown tick, linear volume fade, and auto-restart logic are
      independently authored. These files are NOT subject to the MPL-2.0.

